\subsection{Statistical Validation}

Discrimination collapse depends on attention-mass-based importance scoring shared by major KV cache methods (H$_2$O \cite{h2o-neurips2023}, SnapKV \cite{snapkv-neurips2024}, PyramidKV \cite{pyramidkv-2024}), suggesting broad applicability. Extended discussion in Appendix~\ref{app:extended-discussion}.

\paragraph{Architecture-dependent magnitude.}
Cross-architecture validation on DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B (LlamaForCausalLM) confirms the qualitative pattern---monotonically increasing severity gradient under importance-based eviction with within-strategy phase gradient $d_z \geq 1.0$---while revealing that absolute severity magnitudes are architecture-dependent (${\sim}40{\times}$ smaller than DeepSeek, ${\sim}7{\times}$ smaller than Qwen). This dissociation between consistent directional trends and variable magnitudes suggests the phase-strategy interaction is a general property of compound sparsity on reasoning models, while its quantitative impact depends on architecture-specific attention distributions and head specialization patterns. % exp_id: c3_llama
